  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 233 AM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nThe lingering low will gradually move east on Sunday with\nsurface high pressure arriving in its wake. We'll gradually\nstart to see a warming trend as the August sun modifies the air\nmass and modest ridging replaces the departing trough. By\nmidweek temperatures will be warming back up closer to normal,\nin the upper 80s to low 90s.\n\nConsidering the position and trajectory of the incoming surface\nhigh, moisture return from the Gulf will be shut off through \nmidweek. There's some discrepancy in guidance on how high \ndewpoints get with a skewed distribution in ensemble guidance. \nMost raw model guidance is relatively modest in the 60s, while \nNBM is at the top of the available guidance in the low to mid \n70s. This seems to be driven largely by the bias corrections in \nNBM. If these higher dewpoints do occur, then we could be \nlooking at another period of 100+ heat index values developing. \nHowever, our confidence in this is lowered due to the surface \nhigh blocking moisture from the Gulf, limiting moisture \nincreases locally to evapotranspiration and moisture pooling \nahead of a potential front later in the week. It's that next \nfront in the Thursday-Friday time period that represents our \nnext best chance for rainfall.",
